#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124239 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "6aed23e0-cd3e-5940-a722-63550bcefc97" :question/math-academy-id "e-5431" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n    Notice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124240 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation With Rearranging"}] :question/id #uuid "521cc49e-dddb-5add-b619-18e2785049f8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5432" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124241 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "656da168-af12-53c2-8add-2c82cf71b31c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "77bd52ee-454e-5794-83e5-991e7e4c13b5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5433" :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is $[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124242 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd0537f8-b091-580a-974e-8e928d54939d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Transformation Given its Standard Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9c8d9615-6a5d-5b6a-8735-b9b2f58331f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5434" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e73b8bcf-79c2-5326-b396-d7d3e06badaa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices 